---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Contact from "../components/Contact.astro";

const title = "Goals — Aaditya Ananth";
const description = "What I'm working toward, and an honest read on how far off most of it is.";

// Sourced from the expanded goal statement in memory/wiki/entities/aadi.md
// (Aadi's own words, 2026-07-11). The family motivation recorded there is
// deliberately NOT on this page. Aadi decided 2026-08-10 to keep it off a public
// page; it stays available for one-to-one cold emails.
const nearTerm = [
  {
    k: "Undergrad",
    v: "Biomedical engineering at UT Austin. The plan is to get into a lab early rather than wait until I've earned it on paper.",
  },
  {
    k: "Clinical",
    v: "Finish the EMT course, pass the NREMT, and get real hours. I want the patient contact to stay in front of me while I'm doing engineering coursework.",
  },
  {
    k: "Keep building",
    v: "More instruments, ideally ones that end up in someone's hands rather than a poster.",
  },
];
---

<Base title={title} description={description} path="/goals">
  <header class="page-head">
    <h1>Goals</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      The short version is that I want to practice medicine and run a lab at the same time. The
      longer version is below, and I'm aware most of it is a long way off.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="near">
    <h2 class="section-head" id="near">The next four years</h2>
    <dl class="facts">
      {
        nearTerm.map((n) => (
          <div class="fact">
            <dt>{n.k}</dt>
            <dd>{n.v}</dd>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="arc">
    <h2 class="section-head" id="arc">The longer arc</h2>

    <p>
      I want to be an academic neurosurgeon. Not only the operating side of it, though that is the
      part people picture. The version I actually want is a physician-scientist, so that the
      questions I run into treating people are the same questions I take back to a lab, and so that
      teaching is part of the job rather than something I fit around it.
    </p>

    <p>
      Further out I'd like to help build and run academic hospitals focused on neuroscience. That
      means treating healthcare delivery as a design problem, and using technology and systems work
      to fix things that are currently broken for reasons that have nothing to do with medicine.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="why">
    <h2 class="section-head" id="why">What I actually care about</h2>

    <p>
      Access, more than anything else. My independent study spent nine months on a version of this
      question, looking at how neurologist supply, insurance rates and regional politics in Texas
      line up with who ends up getting care and who doesn't. The finding that stuck with me is how
      little of it is about medicine.
    </p>

    <p>
      So the goal underneath the other goals is expanding access to neurological care for people who
      currently do not have it, and training the people who come after me to do the same. That last
      part matters to me. I have had good mentors and I know exactly how much difference they made.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="caveat">
    <h2 class="section-head" id="caveat">An honest note</h2>
    <p class="caveat">
      I haven't started college yet and none of this is decided. Writing it down is a way of being
      accountable to it, not a claim that it's going to happen. If you're reading this in a few
      years and it's changed, that's probably a good sign.
    </p>
  </section>

  <Contact lead="If you work on any of this, I'd like to hear from you." />
</Base>

<style>
  .page-head {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .page-head h1 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .facts {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .fact {
    padding: var(--space-md) 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-faint);
  }

  .fact:first-child {
    border-top: 0;
    padding-top: 0;
  }

  .fact dt {
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xs);
  }

  .fact dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink-dim);
  }

  @media (min-width: 40rem) {
    .fact {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 8rem 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-lg);
      align-items: baseline;
    }

    .fact dt {
      margin-bottom: 0;
      text-align: right;
    }
  }

  .caveat {
    color: var(--muted);
    border-left: 0;
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
</style>
